      "id": "c245qw7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Chemical Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chemical reactions involve the breaking and forming of chemical bonds between atoms to produce new substances with entirely different properties.",
        "A balanced chemical equation must have an equal number of atoms of each element on both sides to satisfy the Law of Conservation of Mass.",
        "Key indicators of a chemical reaction include temperature change, evolution of a gas, color change, and formation of a precipitate.",
        "Oxidation is defined as the gain of oxygen or loss of hydrogen/electrons, whereas reduction is the loss of oxygen or gain of hydrogen/electrons.",
        "Exothermic reactions release thermal energy to the surroundings, whereas endothermic reactions absorb heat energy."
      ],
      "id": "3yzbrr5"
    },
